# Docker build context excludes for the knowledge-mcp image.
#
# This file is named `dockerignore` here and lands at the published repository
# root as `.dockerignore`. It is a DIFFERENT file from the internal repository's
# own root .dockerignore, which excludes the context for the private cloud and
# static builds — two build contexts, two files, deliberately distinct names so
# neither is mistaken for the other.
#
# Keep this conservative: exclude only what is provably NOT source the build
# needs. The client stage builds the whole module and runs scripts/sync-assets.sh,
# which reads .claude/ and writes internal/assets — so internal/, gen/, go.mod,
# go.sum, .claude/ and scripts/ must all remain in the context.

bin/
.git/
*.log
.DS_Store
